WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:14.900
Macaques in Japan use coins to buy vending
machine snacks.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:21.750
The Dutch village of Giethoorn has no roads;
its buildings are connected entirely by canals

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.670
and footbridges.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:30.500
Beijing, Seoul and Tokyo all mean 'capital'
in their respective languages.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.110
The youngest Pope was 11 years old.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.239
All blue-eyed people are mutants.

00:00:37.239 --> 00:00:42.930
The first ones appeared as recently as 5,000
years ago.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:48.810
More than 90% of all the blackcurrants grown
in Britain go into Ribena.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:56.870
The International Space Station has cost more
than 30 times its own weight in gold.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:08.650
There are 4,800 species of frog in the world
but only one of them goes 'ribbit'.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.160
The amount of water on Earth is constant,
and continually recycled over time: some of

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:22.460
the water you drink will, at one point, have
passed through a dinosaur.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:28.460
Almost all the botox in the world is made
in a single factory in Ireland.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:35.350
Every human being starts out life as an arsehole:
it's the first part of the body to form in

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:36.350
the womb.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:42.840
Mushrooms are more closely related to humans
than to plants.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:46.060
Cocks don't have cocks.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:51.410
In 97% of bird species, the males don't have
penises.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:57.910
3% of pet owners give Valentine's gifts to
their pets on Valentine's Day.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:05.920
At least 109 journeys between adjacent London
Tube stations are quicker to walk.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:11.750
It costs more to make the cardboard box that
Shredded Wheat comes in than it does to make

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:17.310
the Shredded Wheat itself.

